WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.800
The migration runs in eleven
phases, zero through ten.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.153
Each has prerequisites,
steps, validation criteria,

3
00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:10.116
a rollback procedure
and a duration estimate,

4
00:00:10.116 --> 00:00:14.950
and a phase starts only when the previous
one's validation criteria are met.

5
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.459
The durations are planning estimates,

6
00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:21.300
not measured results; the total
runs forty to seventy weeks.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.544
Phase zero is assessment: the forest
and identity inventories in Git, a UPN

8
00:00:26.544 --> 00:00:30.412
remediation plan, a recorded
decision for every group,

9
00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:33.163
and every service account classified.

10
00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:38.621
Phase one deploys sync: at least two Cloud
Sync agents, or Connect where required,

11
00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:40.109
password hash sync on,

12
00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:44.575
validated by object counts within
one percent and no sync errors.

13
00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:48.937
Rollback removes objects from
scope, recoverable for thirty days.

14
00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:53.535
Phase two sets the sign-in method and
puts every Conditional Access policy

15
00:00:53.535 --> 00:00:57.688
in report-only, with the emergency
account sign-in tested and logged.

16
00:00:57.688 --> 00:01:03.201
Phase three migrates groups, with dynamic
membership validated within two percent.

17
00:01:03.201 --> 00:01:06.834
Phase four modernizes service
accounts, high-risk first,

18
00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:10.700
running old and new credentials
in parallel for thirty days.

19
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.246
Phase five rolls out PIM:

20
00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:16.575
zero permanent active assignments
except the emergency accounts.

21
00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:21.188
Phase six enforces Conditional
Access in waves, but only after MFA

22
00:01:21.188 --> 00:01:26.137
registration passes ninety-five
percent in each targeted population.

23
00:01:26.137 --> 00:01:28.955
Phase seven is the
phishing-resistant roadmap,

24
00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:34.300
validated by every privileged account on
FIDO2 or certificate-based authentication,

25
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.984
over eighty percent of managed-device
users on Windows Hello,

26
00:01:37.984 --> 00:01:42.101
and over seventy percent of all
users on a phishing-resistant method.

27
00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:45.438
Phase eight cuts off legacy
authentication after

28
00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.775
thirty consecutive days
with zero legacy sign-ins.

29
00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:52.483
Phase nine decommissions
federation, where it exists:

30
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:56.438
staged rollout moves users to
password hash sync in waves,

31
00:01:56.438 --> 00:02:00.806
then each domain is converted to
managed with Graph PowerShell,

32
00:02:00.806 --> 00:02:06.162
never the retired MSOnline cmdlet, and
AD FS stays recoverable for ninety days.

33
00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:10.450
Phase ten is steady-state governance:
workflows, access packages,

34
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.910
reviews and drift detection running, and
the operations runbook committed to Git.
